er Logic**\n\nI am currently writing a Python script that represents the graph and uses a SAT solver to find an independent set of at least 17 vertices. The script will output the solution as a 0/1 vector if found, or indicate its absence.\n\n**Generating Solver Input**\n\nI am now focused on translating the graph's adjacency list into the DIMACS CNF format. This will prepare the input for the chosen SAT solver, enabling it to search for the independent set of at least 17 vertices.\n\n**Constructing Graph Representation**\n\nI am now focused on building a comprehensive Python representation of the provided graph data. This involves parsing the list of edges and vertices to create an adjacency list or matrix structure suitable for the independent set finding algorithm.\n\n\n---\n**Refactoring the Code**\n\nI've decided to abandon `networkx` completely, realizing I can directly leverage `pysat` for this task. Using `pysat.solvers.RC2` and `pysat.formula.WCNF` seems more direct. I'm actively rewriting the script to reflect this new approach.\n\n\n\n---\n**Confirming Impossibility**\n\nI've determined the maximum independent set size is 9, not the sought-after 17. Consequently, I see no valid set meeting the problem's criteria, rendering it UNSATISFIABLE. I'm now verifying this logical conclusion against the code to ensure the algorithm aligns with the math.\n\n\n", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "native_finish_reason": "STOP", "refusal": null, "correct": true, "satisfiability_correct": true, "solution_correct": true, "validation_details": "Correct UNSAT", "prompt_tokens": 41111, "completion_tokens": 13180, "reasoning_tokens": 2833, "cached_tokens": 16208, "cost_usd": 0.2112076, "cost_source": "openrouter", "latency_ms": 126280.08341789246, "tool_dispatch_ms_total": 1048.6268997192383, "tool_calls_made": 5, "tool_rounds": 5, "n_execute_python": 4, "n_submit_answer": 1, "tool_call_chain": [{"name": "execute_python", "args": {"code": "import networkx as nx\nfrom pysat.sol